title: Start
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 2
position: 0,0
---
This lesson is about the "random" statement, which varies a node's output from one run to the next.

<<random>>
Hey there!
<<or>>
Hi, good to see you!
<<or>>
Hello again!
<<endrandom>>

[[Show me weights.|Weights]]
===
title: Weights
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 0
position: 320,0
---
Each clause can carry a weight. This one is picked about twice as often as the others.

<<random weight="2">>
This is the heavy clause.
<<or weight="1">>
This is a light clause.
<<or>>
This clause uses the default weight of 1.
<<endrandom>>

[[Can a clause do more than text?|Nested]]
===
title: Nested
tags:
speaker: Martin McOwl
colorId: 0
position: 640,0
---
A clause may contain other statements. One of the two branches below sets a variable and shows a conditional line.

<<random>>
<<set $mood = "cheerful">>
<<if $mood == "cheerful">>
  Today I am feeling cheerful.
<<endif>>
<<or>>
<<set $mood = "grumpy">>
Today I am feeling $mood.
<<endrandom>>

[[That is all.|End]]
